{
  "requirement": "The book preprocessor MUST escape requirement names and link targets when inserting badge HTML. It MUST encode badge label and message text in Shields.io URL path components so punctuation cannot change the badge URL structure.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has two obligations. The tests cover both.\n\n**1. Escape requirement names and link targets in inserted badge HTML**\n- `src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[badge_urls_percent_encode_punctuation_and_html_is_escaped]` passes `<`, `>`, `\"`, `'` and `&` into `shield_badge`. It asserts the escaped `alt` text exactly: `&amp;`, `&lt;`, `&gt;`, `&quot;` and `&#39;`.\n- `src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[reference_link_targets_are_escaped]` gives the target chapter a rendered path containing `&`, `\"` and `<x>`. It renders a `{cite}` reference badge from `reference_badge`. It asserts the exact escaped `href`, `a&amp;b &quot;q&quot; &lt;x&gt;.html#habeas-req-rules.ready`. It also asserts that the raw `\"q\"` and `<x>` are absent.\n- `src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[definition_evidence_link_targets_are_escaped]` covers the requirement-name badge link built in `replace_definitions`. It uses an index chapter with a special-character path. It asserts the escaped `href`, the `title` text, and the absence of the raw characters.\n- Requirement names are not tested with HTML-special characters inside `replace_definitions`. The implementation notes that `valid_name` rejects such names. Because of that, no valid input reaches that case, and a test for it would be an edge case the text does not name.\n\n**2. Encode badge label and message text in Shields.io URL path components**\n- `badge_urls_percent_encode_punctuation_and_html_is_escaped` asserts the exact URL. Label `a/b?c` becomes `a%2Fb%3Fc`. Message `x#y%z&w<v>\"u' café` becomes `x%23y%25z%26w%3Cv%3E%22u%27_caf%C3%A9`. So `/`, `?`, `#`, `%`, `&`, `<`, `>`, quotes, the space-to-underscore mapping and non-ASCII are all checked. The test therefore shows that punctuation cannot alter the URL structure.\n- `src/lib.rs#mod[tests]/fn[shields_badge_urls_escape_requirement_names]` asserts that `_` becomes `__` and `-` becomes `--` in the message. It also asserts that a space becomes `_` in `Determination false`.\n\nThe assertions compare exact expected strings, so they would catch the violations this requirement forbids. No marking gaps or acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "f360114568ba3231c5da9e9b2c91d05137e8af13c41c17d23dea91167c755e21",
